  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Lebanon Task Force 01-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Lebanese Task Force, organized by the Near East South Asia Center for Strategic Studies (NESA) is by-name only invitation. This program is designed to continue a conversation with Lebanese CMED participants about the pressing issues in today&apos;s Lebanon; priorities that need to be addressed; and prospects for the immediate and mid-term future. The basic question to be examined: What do Lebanese want Lebanon to be, and what are the next steps moving ahead? The Lebanese only intense RT discussion on 19 Feb follows 2 days (20-24 hrs) of broader security discussions. The meeting will be held under Chatham House Rule, by-name invitation only.</narrative>
  </description>
